    <briefdescription>
<para>Minimal key-value persistence interface for rotation state. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The core protocol is string-key / string-value (get/put). The SecurityLevel-based convenience methods (save/load) are implemented in this base class using the standard key format: &quot;user_storage:rotation_state:{level_name}&quot; → JSON {&quot;last_check_ms&quot;: N}</para>
<para>Allows any backend (in-memory, file-backed, RocksDB, …) to persist rotation state without coupling the scheduler to a specific storage. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
